      ],
      "docs": "The `convohop` object a push carries, with only the fields the contract defines for its type."
    },
    {
      "name": "PushNotificationType",
      "kind": "type",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#PushNotificationType",
      "anchor": "pushnotificationtype-type",
      "signatures": [
        "type PushNotificationType = \"notification.message\" | \"notification.call\" | \"notification.callCancelled\""
      ],
      "docs": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "PushRegistration",
      "kind": "type",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#PushRegistration",
      "anchor": "pushregistration-type",
      "signatures": [
        "type PushRegistration = {\n    readonly kind: \"webPush\";\n    readonly subscription: WebPushSubscription;\n} | {\n    readonly kind: \"apns\" | \"apnsVoip\";\n    readonly token: string;\n    readonly environment?: \"development\" | \"production\";\n} | {\n    readonly kind: \"fcm\";\n    readonly token: string;\n    readonly fid?: never;\n} | {\n    readonly kind: \"fcm\";\n    readonly fid: string;\n    readonly token?: never;\n}"
      ],
      "docs": "Where your backend sends one device's pushes. Every ConvoHop client hands your app this shape, so one backend\nendpoint can store registrations from browsers and native apps. ConvoHop never sees them.\n\n- `webPush`: a browser subscription; your backend signs pushes with its VAPID private key.\n- `apns`: an iOS device token for alerts. `environment` says which APNs host accepts it, when the app knows.\n- `apnsVoip`: an iOS PushKit token for incoming calls.\n- `fcm`: an Android app's Firebase Cloud Messaging target, with exactly one of `token` and `fid`. `token` is the\n  registration token, which apps get by default. `fid` is the Firebase Installation ID, which apps get instead when\n  their manifest sets `firebase_messaging_installation_id_enabled`. Send to it with the FCM HTTP v1 target of the\n  same name."
    },
    {
      "name": "defaultWebNotification",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#defaultWebNotification",
      "anchor": "defaultwebnotification-function",
      "signatures": ["function defaultWebNotification(action: NotificationAction): WebNotification"],
      "docs": "The default presentation. It uses the title and body your backend set, with English fallback titles, and the\naction's tag, so a duplicate or a stopped ring replaces its earlier notification. A ring stays until it is handled;\na ring that stopped without being missed is replaced silently."
    },
    {
      "name": "handleNotification",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#handleNotification",
      "anchor": "handlenotification-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function handleNotification(payload: unknown, now?: number): NotificationAction"
      ],
      "docs": "`NotificationHandler.handle` with a handler shared by this module."
    },
    {
      "name": "handleNotificationClick",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#handleNotificationClick",
      "anchor": "handlenotificationclick-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function handleNotificationClick(clients: WebClients, event: WebNotificationClickEvent, url: (notification: PushNotification, action: string | undefined) => string): boolean"
      ],
      "docs": "Handles a `notificationclick` for a ConvoHop notification: closes it, then focuses a window already showing `url`\nor opens one. `url` maps the notification (and the clicked action, if any) to a URL of your app: relative to the\nservice worker, such as `/conversations/${notification.conversationId}`, or absolute on its origin. Another origin\nis a TypeError, and the notification stays open. Returns whether the notification was a ConvoHop one."
    },
    {
      "name": "handlePushEvent",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#handlePushEvent",
      "anchor": "handlepushevent-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function handlePushEvent(registration: ServiceWorkerRegistration, event: WebPushEvent, options?: WebPushEventOptions): void"
      ],
      "docs": "Handles a service worker `push` event: `self.addEventListener(\"push\", event => handlePushEvent(self.registration, event))`."
    },
    {
      "name": "parsePushNotification",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#parsePushNotification",
      "anchor": "parsepushnotification-function",
      "signatures": ["function parsePushNotification(value: unknown): PushNotification"],
      "docs": "Validates the `convohop` object of a push against the push payload contract. Returns its known fields and ignores\nfields the contract doesn't define for its type. Throws a `TypeError` for anything else."
    },
    {
      "name": "parsePushPayload",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#parsePushPayload",
      "anchor": "parsepushpayload-function",
      "signatures": ["function parsePushPayload(payload: unknown): PushNotification"],
      "docs": "Finds and validates the notification in a push: a Web Push or APNs payload (`{ convohop: {...} }`), FCM data\n(`{ convohop: \"<json>\" }`) or the `convohop` object itself."
    },
    {
      "name": "showPushNotification",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#showPushNotification",
      "anchor": "showpushnotification-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function showPushNotification(registration: ServiceWorkerRegistration, payload: unknown, options?: WebPushHandlerOptions): Promise<NotificationAction>"
      ],
      "docs": "Shows the notification for a decrypted Web Push payload (`event.data.json()`) and returns the action taken.\n\nBrowsers expect every push to show a notification: Safari revokes the subscription after a few pushes that don't,\nand Chrome shows a generic one. So every action, including duplicates and stopped rings, shows or replaces one."
    },
    {
      "name": "subscribePush",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#subscribePush",
      "anchor": "subscribepush-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function subscribePush(registration: ServiceWorkerRegistration, options: WebPushSubscribeOptions): Promise<PushSubscription>"
      ],
      "docs": "Subscribes this browser to Web Push with your VAPID key and registers the subscription with your backend.\nReuses a subscription for the same key and replaces one made with another key. Call it from a user gesture:\nsubscribing asks for notification permission, and some browsers only ask from a gesture."
    },
    {
      "name": "unsubscribePush",
      "kind": "function",
      "ref": "@convohop/client/push#unsubscribePush",
      "anchor": "unsubscribepush-function",
      "signatures": [
        "function unsubscribePush(registration: ServiceWorkerRegistration, unregister?: (registration: PushRegistration) => Promise<void> | void): Promise<boolean>"
      ],
      "docs": "Unsubscribes this browser and, first, lets your backend forget the subscription. Resolves whether a subscription\nexisted."
    }
  ]
}
